# Infrastructure

Supports `.project-overview.mdc` and `architecture.mdc`. Infrastructure is replaceable. Domain is not rewritten when a vendor changes.

## Outbound adapters

Implement application ports only:

- `PostgresConversationRepository` → `ConversationRepository`
- TypeScript: Prisma/PostgreSQL, Redis, email, WhatsApp, queues, `PythonAIServiceAdapter` (`AIServicePort`)
- Python AI: LLM / embedding / vector-store providers under `adapters/llm/`, `adapters/embeddings/`, `adapters/vector_store/` — never Prisma. Do not install every provider now.

Map Prisma records ↔ domain entities in the adapter. Never return Prisma models to use cases or domain.

## Inbound adapters

REST, WebSocket, webhooks, queue consumers, event consumers: parse → authorize → use case → map response.

No business rules, no Prisma, no LLM SDKs in inbound adapters. FastAPI handlers in `apps/ai` stay thin the same way. TypeScript inbound adapters must not call OpenAI, LangChain, LangGraph, or LlamaIndex.

## Redis

Use for cache, rate limits, queues, temporary state, distributed locks. Not the primary transactional store.

## Reliability

Important state changes that emit events use the Outbox in the same database transaction. Consumers are idempotent. Do not dual-write business state and a queue without an outbox.
